WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.730
- Our next guest has been in our lives

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.820
since she was a little girl,

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.000
with movies like "How the
Grinch Stole Christmas"

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.560
and shows like "Gossip Girl."

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.560
She's also a very talented musician,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.290
her band is called The Pretty Reckless.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.940
They are nominated for
two iHeartRadio Awards.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.550
They are the only
female-fronted band nominated

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.343
in their categories,

00:00:17.343 --> 00:00:20.090
and their latest album hit
number one on the rock charts,

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.840
which is so cool for a
chick, I'm just saying.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.490
It's called "Death by Rock and Roll."

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.930
Let's say hello to
Taylor Momsen, everybody!

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.124
(upbeat music)

00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:30.957
Hi!

00:00:30.957 --> 00:00:32.070
- Hey Kelly, how are you?

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.282
- I am so good!

00:00:33.282 --> 00:00:34.850
I am so proud of you,
I don't even know you,

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.160
but that was so cool on the rock charts!

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.080
That rarely happens for
women, let's be real.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.351
- Unfortunately, yeah, rare.
- [Kelly] A rarity.

00:00:43.351 --> 00:00:46.470
- And I believe "Death by Rock and Roll,"

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:47.710
we actually just set an,

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.519
well, "Death by Rock and Roll" the single,

00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:54.260
went number one, which is crazy in Covid,

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.430
to put out a song and
have it go number one

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.833
and not be able to play it live.

00:00:57.833 --> 00:00:58.666
- Yeah.

00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:02.610
- And then, our latest
single "And So It Went"

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.440
which features the amazing Tom Morello

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.150
also just reached number one,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.090
so I believe that makes it
our sixth number one single

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.440
at the rock format, which--
- [Kelly] What?!

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.550
- So, yeah, I think we're
breaking records, I think we,

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.190
not to like tout myself--
- I'm so sorry for you!

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.930
You're not even able to, like, play this,

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.310
like the energy when you
get a number one song

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.970
and you're playing live.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:26.420
I'm so sorry, that sucks, Covid! Yeah.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.860
- Well, yeah. You know,
but what're you gonna do?

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.620
We're all in the same boat.
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.790
- We're just hanging in, being patient,

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:36.640
and just so thankful and
so grateful to all the fans

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.724
and everyone who's listened,

00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:41.500
and radio stations and
everyone who's played it,

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.200
like it's just absolutely
incredible to see it.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.706
And I've now, I'm trying to
become like a tech-type person,

00:01:49.706 --> 00:01:53.956
I'm still really bad at
it, if I'm being honest.

00:01:53.956 --> 00:01:57.060
But I've now discovered
that there's these things

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.362
called reaction videos online--

00:01:59.362 --> 00:02:00.195
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:02:00.195 --> 00:02:03.680
- Where you can, like, watch
people videotape themselves

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.051
listening to a song, or your
song for the first time.

00:02:09.051 --> 00:02:10.980
And it's not even about what they say,

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.840
but watching their face
as they listen to it

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.880
I found very enjoyable.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.181
And so in lieu of a massive
audience in front of you,

00:02:21.181 --> 00:02:23.925
that's been something that's
become a hobby of mine.

00:02:23.925 --> 00:02:25.520
- It's the next best thing, yeah!

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.870
It feels like it's like, okay,
people are listening to it,

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.770
it's like a show of some form
in my head, in my brain movie.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:32.684
But what was the process
like for this album?

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:35.930
Was it different than
recording the other albums?

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.430
- I mean it was different, yeah,

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:38.750
it was different in a lot of ways.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.096
I mean, not to get too heavy,

00:02:40.096 --> 00:02:44.620
but we went through a lot of
loss in the past few years.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.400
So to, sorry, to make a
very long story short,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.451
I fell very dark into a hole of depression

00:02:51.451 --> 00:02:54.790
and everything that comes with
loss and trauma and grief,

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.163
and I wasn't really sure
how to get out of it,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:03.949
and, really, as cliche as
it may sound, it was music.

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:06.970
Music was the thing that
really brought me back to life,

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.833
and brought the sparkle back into my eyes.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.690
- [Kelly] It's therapeutic.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:16.033
- Super therapeutic, and
the writing of the record,

00:03:17.081 --> 00:03:18.260
it just, like, the floodgates opened

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.300
and this record kind of wrote itself

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.670
whether I wanted it to or not.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.660
I didn't really have a
choice in the matter.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.980
And I wasn't even thinking
about recording it

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.380
or putting it out, I wasn't
thinking that far ahead.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.690
It just flowed,

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.700
and I think that makes for
something that's really special.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.630
And, even the title,
"Death by Rock and Roll"

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.280
which I know can sound very
morbid to a lot of people

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.280
just because of the title, just
because of the word 'death,'

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.410
is not, like, "Death by Rock
and Roll" was this motto,

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:52.810
and this ethic, and this lifestyle,

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.140
that was like, live your life by,

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.610
of live life your own
way, go out your own way,

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.300
don't let anyone tell you differently,

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.330
don't let anyone tell you
how to live, like, freedom.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:06.840
So it was very much like a
battle cry for life itself.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:11.182
And so, that phrase just
started to resonate in my head

00:04:11.182 --> 00:04:15.103
in a way that I couldn't ignore, I guess,

00:04:16.227 --> 00:04:18.803
and in a new way, I guess.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.450
You know, I hope people
can relate to that,

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.340
and maybe kind of find some solace in it

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.610
the same way I found solace

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.070
in the records that I grew
up loving and listening to,

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:32.845
and finding that comfort, and
knowing that you're not alone.

00:04:32.845 --> 00:04:35.077
- Absolutely! Yeah, knowing
that you're not alone.

00:04:35.077 --> 00:04:36.410
- And things do get better.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.940
- Yeah. Well thank you so much, Taylor!

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:39.960
It's great to meet you!

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.960
I cannot wait to hear this whole record.

